  "all_ingredients_flat": "opo squash, zucchini, besan, gram flour, chickpea flour, ground flaxseed, salt, black pepper powder, red chili powder, ajwain, carom seeds, turmeric, Trader Joe's Herb de Provence, oregano",
  "instructions": "BATTER: Shred medium size opo squash ('laud' / 'doodhi') or zucchini. Mix 1 cup 'besan' (gram flour / chickpea flour), about 2 tsp ground flaxseed, salt (to taste), black pepper powder, red chili powder & 'ajwain' (carom seeds). Mix well. Batter consistency should allow us to shape it into loose balls. KOFTA: Air fry both sides at 400F for 10 minutes each. For a crispier texture, air fry for a longer duration.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "air-fry"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "",
  "notes": "TIP: \"Today, I ran out of ajwain and replaced it with 1 tsp Trader Joe's Herb de Provence and it tasted very good. Oregano has a flavor similar to ajwain.\"",
